# The shared language policy (MWBM-MEDIA-LANG) — exact copies, byte for byte
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These files are copies of master files in MWBMPartners/MeedyaSuite-core.
# scripts/media-lang/check_copies.py (run by CI) compares each one's SHA-256
# checksum with the lock file and with the master. A single changed byte
# fails that check.
#
# The settings on each line below stop git changing a copy's bytes through
# line-ending conversion (-text: a Windows checkout turning every "\n" into
# "\r\n"), through a filter (-filter), through text-encoding conversion
# (-working-tree-encoding), or through "$Id$" expansion (-ident).
#
# What can still override them, by git's own rules for attributes:
#   - any LATER line in this same file that also matches a copy. Git uses
#     the last matching line for each setting, so that line need not be
#     broader than these to win;
#   - a .gitattributes file closer to the copy: in the copy's own folder, or
#     in a folder between it and the top of the repository (a deeper file
#     wins over a shallower one). A .gitattributes in some other folder, one
#     that does not contain the copy, has no effect on it;
#   - .git/info/attributes on somebody's own machine, because git always
#     gives that file the highest priority.
# The global and system attributes files have the LOWEST priority, so they
# cannot override these lines. Whatever overrides them, the copy checker
# still compares every byte and reports a changed copy as changed.
#
# Never edit the copies. Change the master in MeedyaSuite-core, then take it
# here with: python3 scripts/media-lang/check_copies.py --update <commit>
#
# The lock file is written by the checker rather than copied, but it is read
# back line by line, so it gets the same protection.
docs/standards/media-language-bcp47-policy.md -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
docs/standards/data/bcp47-language-data-v1.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
docs/standards/data/bcp47-language-data-v1.schema.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
tests/fixtures/bcp47-language-policy-v1.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
tests/fixtures/bcp47-language-policy-v1.schema.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
scripts/media-lang/check_copies.py -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
docs/standards/MWBM-MEDIA-LANG.lock -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
